---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { contactLink } from '../site';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Parts Relay for repair shops | Send parts requests to your distributor"
  description="How repair shops use Parts Relay: search parts by sending your distributor a WhatsApp message with the plate or VIN and the part, and what to put in it."
>
  <div class="team-page team-shops">
    <section class="team-hero">
      <div class="team-frame">
        <p class="team-label">For repair shops</p>
        <h1 tabindex="-1">Parts Relay for repair shops</h1>
        <p class="team-hero-note">
          If your distributor uses Parts Relay and has enabled your workshop as a contact, your
          advisers can search parts by sending it a WhatsApp message with the plate or VIN and the
          part they need. Below is what to put in that request so the counter can answer it.
        </p>
        <div class="team-actions">
          <a class="team-btn" href={contactLink}>
            Talk to our team
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-section team-shop-intro">
      <div class="team-frame team-intake">
        <div>
          <p class="team-label">At the service desk</p>
          <h2 class="team-h2">The shop needs a rear caliper. Does it come with the carrier?</h2>
          <p>
            A request for “rear brakes” leaves the counter to work out whether you mean a pad set, a
            caliper or its carrier. If the technician has already identified the caliper, put that
            on the enquiry.
          </p>
          <p>
            Get the side and parking-brake mechanism from the bay while the car is there. If you are
            waiting on either detail, say which one.
          </p>
        </div>
        <section class="team-record">
          <h3>A note for the distributor</h3>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Vehicle details</dt>
              <dd>
                Record the vehicle identifier from the repair order and confirm it against the car.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>On the repair order</dt>
              <dd>One rear brake caliper</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>From the technician</dt>
              <dd>Confirm the side and the parking-brake mechanism fitted to the car.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Question for the quote</dt>
              <dd>
                “Does your caliper include the carrier, or should I add it as a separate item?”
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-section team-principles">
      <div class="team-frame">
        <p class="team-label">Writing the enquiry</p>
        <h2 class="team-h2">Before you call the distributor</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <div class="team-principle-name">
              <span>
                <svg
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.35"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m3 13 2-5h12l4 5v5H3zM3 13h18M6 18v2m12-2v2M6 15h2m8 0h2" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <h3>Check the vehicle in the bay</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Take the VIN from the vehicle in the bay. Read the model back against the repair order
              before you send it.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="team-principle-name">
              <span>
                <svg
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.35"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m12 2 8 4v11l-8 5-8-5V6zM4 6l8 5 8-5m-8 5v11M8 4l8 5" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <h3>Use the technician’s part name</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              If the note says “mirror cap,” keep those words. Changing it to “mirror” could get you
              a quote for the whole unit.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="team-principle-name">
              <span>
                <svg
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.35"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="M3 4h9l9 9-8 8-10-10z" />
                  <circle cx="7.5" cy="8" r="1.2" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <h3>Say where it fits</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Give the axle and side when they matter. For an electrical part, ask whether the
              technician can read the old number or describe the plug.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="team-principle-name">
              <span>
                <svg
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.35"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="M3 4h18v12H10l-5 4v-4H3zM7 8h10M7 12h6" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <h3>Ask about the box</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Tell the counter if the repair depends on an extra fitting. For a caliper, ask whether
              the carrier comes with it.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-section">
      <div class="team-frame team-intake">
        <div>
          <p class="team-label">Sending it in</p>
          <h2 class="team-h2">How your request reaches the desk</h2>
          <p>
            If the distributor has added your WhatsApp number as a contact, send the plate or VIN
            and the part you need to its Parts Relay number. A number that has not been added gets a
            reply asking it to contact the distributor. For a search at the counter, give the person
            at the desk the plate or VIN and the part.
          </p>
        </div>
        <section class="team-record">
          <h3>When the counter gets back to you</h3>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Vehicle identified</dt>
              <dd>
                Read the model and engine. Let the counter know if either differs from the car on
                the lift.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>References returned</dt>
              <dd>
                Put the original part code beside its description on the estimate. Some results also
                have a drawing or an aftermarket reference.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Nothing matched</dt>
              <dd>
                A missing vehicle calls for another look at the plate. If the vehicle is right, ask
                the technician for a more precise part name or location.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-section team-shop-start" id="team-shop-start" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="team-frame">
        <p class="team-label">At the estimate stage</p>
        <h2 class="team-h2">Before you give the customer a date</h2>
        <div class="team-shop-example">
          <div>
            <h3>Put the technician’s wording on the enquiry</h3>
            <p>
              Write down the part, side and original number while the technician has the car, and
              put all three in the message to your distributor.
            </p>
            <a class="team-btn" href="/tools/vin-check/">
              Check the VIN
            </a>
          </div>
          <section class="team-record">
            <h3>What belongs on the estimate</h3>
            <dl>
              <div>
                <dt>Fit</dt>
                <dd>
                  Make sure the counter checked the position and equipment fitted to this car.
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>Kit contents</dt>
                <dd>Give a separately supplied seal, sensor or fitting its own line.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>Availability</dt>
                <dd>Get the quantity and collection or delivery time from the supplying branch.</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <ContactBand />
  </div>
</Layout>
